1	/**
2	 * A Behavior has two cursors and they advance by different rules.
3	 *
4	 * The SCHEDULE cursor (`watchers.next_run_at`) is recomputed from `now`, so a
5	 * missed occurrence is never replayed. The WINDOW cursor
6	 * (`max(canvas_windows.window_start)`) advances one period per COMPLETED window
7	 * and is capped at the current period but never jumps to it. Wall-clock moves
8	 * one period per period, so once a Behavior falls behind it stays behind: the
9	 * gap is frozen, not closed.
10	 *
11	 * Prod Behavior 2 ("HN engagement — draft replies", daily) measured 2026-08-06:
12	 * newest window `2026-06-17`, written by a run on `2026-07-15`. Drift by window,
13	 * monotonic — covers 06-06 written 06-11 (5d), 06-14 written 06-27 (13d), 06-15
14	 * written 07-08 (23d), 06-17 written 07-15 (28d). It was not failing: those late
15	 * windows carry `content_analyzed = 40`. It read forty real Hacker News stories
16	 * and drafted real replies to threads a month dead, and reported success.
17	 *
18	 * Nothing told it. The dispatch said "your window is June 17" and never that
19	 * today was August 6 — from inside a run a stale window is indistinguishable
20	 * from a fresh one. These tests pin the facts now reported, and the alignment of
21	 * a span the agent picks for itself.
22	 */
