1	/**
2	 * Window rollover for scheduled Behaviors.
3	 *
4	 * `canvas_windows` is a VIEW over `canvas_state` event chains: one row per chain
5	 * ROOT, content from the chain HEAD. The ROOT carries the period. So "did the
6	 * window roll over" is really "did a new root get created", and the only thing
7	 * that decides it is the (window_start, granularity) pair the run is dispatched
8	 * with — `findCanvasHead` matches on it, and a match means supersede-in-place
9	 * instead of a new period.
10	 *
11	 * The bug this pins: `computePendingWindow` chained the next window off the
12	 * previous window's `window_end`. That is only correct if `window_end` is an
13	 * EXCLUSIVE boundary, and prod stores both conventions in one table (measured
14	 * 2026-07-31: daily 29 inclusive `23:59:59.999` vs 32 exclusive `00:00:00`;
15	 * weekly 28 vs 2). Chaining off an inclusive end starts the next window at
16	 * `…T23:59:59.999Z` — a day minus a millisecond off — and 14 of 102 prod
17	 * windows are misaligned that way.
18	 *
19	 * Two distinct failures fall out, both silent:
20	 *
21	 *  1. The `windowEnd > currentPeriodEnd` clamp collapses a misaligned window to
22	 *     ZERO duration (`23:59:59.999` → `00:00:00`). Five such windows exist on
23	 *     prod and all five have `content_analyzed = 0` — a Behavior that analyzed
24	 *     nothing and reported success.
25	 *  2. The misaligned start never matches a fresh period, so no new root is
26	 *     created, so `lastWindow` never advances, so the scheduler re-dispatches
27	 *     the same window forever. Behavior 71 ran hourly for a full day writing
28	 *     into the previous day's window (dispatched `2026-07-30T23:59:59.999Z`,
29	 *     wrote `2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z`).
30	 *
31	 * The fix must ALSO not run away in the other direction: granularity has no
32	 * 'hourly' (`BEHAVIOR_TIME_GRANULARITIES` is daily/weekly/monthly/quarterly),
33	 * so an hourly cron necessarily gets a DAILY window and must re-dispatch the
34	 * SAME period all day. "Always advance one period" would mint tomorrow's window
35	 * at 00:01 and march into the future.
